Workstation SLURM: users are the same user by name, not by uid (each machine has its own
accounts, so uids differ between machines). A uid is only a name's number on one machine:
where SLURM needs a number (signing, running a job) it's the local one; where it matches or
shows users, it uses names. Applied by build.sh. See the comments in the code, and
SLURM/Setup.md ("Users and uids").

Doesn't fix:
- squeue -s -u (steps by user) matches by number: only right on the controller's machine.
- squeue --json/--yaml and squeue -s name users from the local number: elsewhere, someone else's.
- Numbers shown or passed on can be another machine's: the uid in scontrol's UserId=name(uid),
  SLURM_JOB_UID/SLURM_JOB_GID (eg. in the Prolog and Epilog). Use names.
- Options taking a uid number (eg. squeue -u 1006) mean that number on the machine they run on.
- Patched and unpatched machines still disagree: every machine needs this build.
- Relies on munged's socket being usable only by the SLURM user: anyone who can use it can
  claim any user name.
- Not checked: accounting, sbcast, X11 forwarding, reservations or partitions by user or group.
Without the patch, uids (not gids) must match on every machine.

